From 7b45fc6288b34e9c215a0d907cd0ef342e316462 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivory <contact@ivory.cafe>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 22:00:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/21] Preserve logical DEX provenance for Fusion rehydration

Capture live DexFile identity and logical data fallback so protected classes can be reconstructed only when complete runtime evidence is available. Reuse the strict host rehydrator and keep checksum-safe partial fallbacks for legacy runs.\n\nConstraint: Manager acceptance does not require a full user image build; host repair must remain conservative on incomplete evidence.\nRejected: Fabricating DEX tables from class names or CodeItems | It cannot produce JADX-safe bytecode or trustworthy references.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate\nDirective: Keep runtime_view provenance and reconstructed_standard_verified trust gates intact when extending capture points.\nTested: Python host/rehydrator regression suite 18/18; py_compile; diff --check.\nNot-tested: Android C++ build blocked by unrelated external/libjxl vendor variant errors during Soong bootstrap.

Change-Id: I06bcb5e4e3a3d05b5ebba1d19f43f4883edc0966
